+research-wiki\retrieval-index\BOOKMAP-CHAPTERS-5-6-CANONICAL-COMPLETION.json:26647:      "role": "Compiled textbook-style positive-gap finite-sum endpoint for the practical selected-policy generated-UCB theorem. For one positive gap g and full peeling budget L, selectedPolicySuccessorTextbookGapBudget is 32*sigma2*L/g + 4*L + 2*g. Nat.ceil_lt_add_one bounds the integer threshold by its real max plus two; nonnegativity of both max branches bounds max by their sum; multiplication by g and field normalization remove one gap power. The ENNReal wrapper transports this inequality with ENNReal.ofReal_natCast, ENNReal.ofReal_mul, and ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal. The finite-arm consumer filters Finset.univ to strictly positive model gaps, preserves the gap*T*ofReal(delta) confidence-failure term exactly, and removes every zero-gap arm using FiniteBanditModel.gap_nonneg. The final theorem composes this algebra with the complete practical selected reward-law pseudo-regret theorem, so its Lean-facing RHS is the positive-gap sum of ofReal(32*sigma2*L/g + 4*L + 2*g) plus ofReal(g)*(T*ofReal(delta)). Regularity contracts are unchanged from the practical theorem: probability and Standard Borel Omega, measurable context/reward/state/mean, trim-a.e. selected reward-coordinate condExpKernel.map law for the generated policy, raw and mean ranges, CenteredRewardKernelLaw, stationary means equal to model.mean, positive uniform selected-history variance, K,T>0, and delta>0. No caller supplies per-arm positivity, threshold, radius, or numeric inversion conditions. Imports/APIs are UCBConditionalRewardLawPolicy, FiniteBanditModelInvariants, ScalarPseudoRegret, Nat.ceil_lt_add_one, max/order and field algebra, Finset.filter/sum, ENNReal.ofReal casts, and the prior explicit-threshold pseudo-regret endpoint. Retrieval evidence is compiled local/Mathlib-backed through LOCAL-LEAF-UCB-SELECTED-POLICY-GENERATED-EXPLICIT-THRESHOLD-PSEUDOREGRET, LOCAL-LEAF-UCB-SELECTED-POLICY-GENERATED-EXPLICIT-THRESHOLD-EXPECTED-PULLCOUNT, MLIB-FINSET-SUMS, MLIB-ORDER-ALGEBRA, and MLIB-MEASURE-INTEGRAL; theorem cards and weapon-only material are not proofs. Status is leanCompiled, root imported through the existing module import, focused-built, externally canaried through Tests.Basic, and consumed by the canonical reward-only trajMeasure endpoint. Failure policy: integer-threshold removal, reciprocal-gap simplification, positive-gap filtering, zero-gap elimination, and the complete practical selected-law ENNReal pseudo-regret theorem are closed. The canonical UCB selected-law producer and canonical reward-only trajMeasure theorem now compile downstream. An optional Real/Bochner wrapper remains separate. No anytime/self-normalized/general Freedman, literal cross-toolchain LML import, or final broad UCB theorem is claimed.",
